From 025bd80b7f24a7554dd304650f20fa74ea4879a6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 16:10:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 15/17] port d9927ecf: generate: opt-in reuse of an idle slot's
 chain (STRATA_SLOT_CHAIN_REUSE) and of a give-back's checkpoints
 (STRATA_GIVEBACK_CHECKS)

Adaptations to v0.2.12:
- E1 (STRATA_SLOT_CHAIN_REUSE): the slot search is the same loop as before, so scan_slot replaces it as in the
  original (switch off: the old loop's pick, slot_chain_test's oracle). The give-back was reworked upstream (#2526,
  cea3ed40: the slot's checkpoints that are prefixes of the tokens copied back come along, the one continued from
  first). A chain hit now goes through that code: the chain checkpoint is copied first, the slot's own shorter
  prefixes are copied (never moved: move_cks is off after a chain hit, the slot keeps its conversation), then
  chain_along's shorter chain checkpoints are copied (deduplicated, out-of-memory skips them like upstream's shorter
  ones), before upstream's fix-up loop points slot_ck into `checks`. The SLOT_PARK discard and chain move are skipped
  after a chain hit, as before. Plain copies (upstream's give-back does not use STRATA_CKPT_POOL there), so the
  original push_copy helper is gone.
- E2 (STRATA_GIVEBACK_CHECKS): upstream's give-back already hands the slot's own prefix checkpoints over without a
  switch (copied; moved with STRATA_SLOT_CKPT_MOVE). What remains of ours is giveback_plan's hand_move: with the switch,
  a give-back of all a slot holds into the slot the request is admitted to moves them through upstream's move_cks
  path instead of copying them, plus the "and N checkpoints of its own" log text. giveback_picks is no longer called
  by the engine; it stays in slot_chain.hpp as the rule's model for slot_chain_test (header comment says so).
- slot_chain.hpp include placed after pipe_probe.hpp, and slot_chain_test after split_walk_test in CMakeLists, so the
  merge with g3-212-vision (mrope_regions next to batch_groups / gguf_geometry_test) does not collide.
- Not in this commit: tools/cache_reuse_check.py (and its fix bbf90765) and the tools/vision_check_fake_engine.py
  hunk. They import tools/vision_batch_check.py and extend the fake engine of f8a41fff, which is only on
  g3-212-vision (3591ee27); they go on top of the integration branch.

Both switches unset: the search picks what upstream's loop picks, move_cks is upstream's expression, the SLOT_PARK
block runs as upstream's and the log line is upstream's.

(cherry picked from commit d9927ecfb2b039d6431f3e1eb426d999aebbecb6)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
